{"uid":"440f40c6e64ea6b8","name":"test_task_scoped_approach_mismatch_stays_historical_for_the_peer_verdict_gate_too","fullName":"tests.test_operator_ruling#test_task_scoped_approach_mismatch_stays_historical_for_the_peer_verdict_gate_too","historyId":"327617b5698458283677d79f9df20599","time":{"start":1791956541079,"stop":1791956541093,"duration":14},"description":"Task 022 (D.13, #196): regression proof that the ordinary,\n    task-scoped case -- an approach-1 ruling that stops binding once\n    approach 2 has replanned around it -- still demotes to 'Historical\n    rulings' for BOTH judging hats, not only for review.\n\n    `test_earlier_approach_ruling_is_historical_not_binding_in_a_later_one`\n    (task 038, #172/#168) already pins this for review, driven through\n    `_review_extra_context()`. D.8 (task 018) later handed the SAME\n    builder to the peer verdict gate, and D.9-D.12 (tasks 019-021) then\n    reshaped the historical bucket underneath both call sites -- so D.13's\n    own 'did not regress' claim is unproven for the verdict-gate audience\n    until something drives it there too. This test does exactly that,\n    through the real `LoopSupervisor._step_verdict_gate()` (never a direct\n    call to `_operator_amendment_review_context()` alone), on a plain\n    task-scoped ruling (no wave scope, unlike\n    `test_wave_scoped_ruling_reaches_the_peer_verdict_gate_after_a_replan`\n    just below, which pins the OPPOSITE disposition -- still binding).\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 022 (D.13, #196): regression proof that the ordinary,<br />\ntask-scoped case -- an approach-1 ruling that stops binding once<br />\napproach 2 has replanned around it -- still demotes to 'Historical<br />\nrulings' for BOTH judging hats, not only for review.</p>\n<pre><code>`test_earlier_approach_ruling_is_historical_not_binding_in_a_later_one`\n(task 038, #172/#168) already pins this for review, driven through\n`_review_extra_context()`. D.8 (task 018) later handed the SAME\nbuilder to the peer verdict gate, and D.9-D.12 (tasks 019-021) then\nreshaped the historical bucket underneath both call sites -- so D.13's\nown 'did not regress' claim is unproven for the verdict-gate audience\nuntil something drives it there too. This test does exactly that,\nthrough the real `LoopSupervisor._step_verdict_gate()` (never a direct\ncall to `_operator_amendment_review_context()` alone), on a plain\ntask-scoped ruling (no wave scope, unlike\n`test_wave_scoped_ruling_reaches_the_peer_verdict_gate_after_a_replan`\njust below, which pins the OPPOSITE disposition -- still binding).\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791956453364,"stop":1791956453364,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791956453365,"stop":1791956453365,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791956541062,"stop":1791956541067,"duration":5},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791956541062,"stop":1791956541062,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791956541067,"stop":1791956541067,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shoul